   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to the sale of certain\nproducts for human consumption",
    "basePrintNo": "S8042",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8042-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Ren §§391-o, 391-r, 391-s & 399-hh to be Art 38-B §§831 - 834, §399-hhh to be §830, add Art 38-B Art Head, amd §830, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.582 & A.6798)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8042\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN-SIGAL\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to the sale of\ncertain products for human consumption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the provisions of\nL.2023 c.753, to clarify provisions exempting foods that comply with\nfederal law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding clarifying\nlanguage that the ban will not apply to foods containing sodium nitrate\nor nitrite in compliance with the federal laws related to use of food\ningredients and sources of radiation as written in 9 CFR Part 424 or 21\nCFR Part 172.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 753 of the Laws of 2023. 5.582 and A.6798\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2023 general business law, in relation to prohib-\niting the sale of sodium nitrate and sodium nitrite to any person under\nthe age of twenty-one, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.582\nand A.6798, takes effect.\n",
